                      },
                    ],
                    "kind": "component",
                    "name": "SectionLabel",
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Nursing documentation moves the revenue cycle in two places you can measure.",
                      },
                    ],
                    "kind": "primitive",
                    "props": {
                      "style": {
                        "color": "#1A1A1A",
                        "fontSize": 22,
                        "fontWeight": "bold",
                        "lineHeight": 1.2,
                        "marginBottom": 8,
                      },
                    },
                    "tag": "TEXT",
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Direct billing originates with the attesting physician or APP — that's a separate model. But nursing documentation is the upstream record that CDI, quality reporting, and payer contracts all read from. These signals do not appear in the financial totals above; they are the leading indicators that confirm the story those totals tell.",
                      },
                    ],
                    "kind": "primitive",
                    "props": {
                      "style": {
                        "color": "#666666",
                        "fontSize": 10.5,
                        "lineHeight": 1.5,
                        "marginBottom": 12,
                      },
                    },
                    "tag": "TEXT",
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "kind": "text",
                                "value": "01",
                              },
                            ],
                            "kind": "primitive",
                            "props": {
                              "style": {
                                "color": "#EA2C00",
                                "fontSize": 10,
                                "fontWeight": "bold",
                                "marginRight": 10,
                                "minWidth": 20,
                              },
                            },
                            "tag": "TEXT",
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "kind": "text",
                                "value": "CDI Query Reduction",
                              },
                            ],
                            "kind": "primitive",
                            "props": {
                              "style": {
                                "color": "#1A1A1A",
                                "flex": 1,
                                "fontSize": 11,
                                "fontWeight": "bold",
                              },
                            },
                            "tag": "TEXT",
                          },
                        ],
                        "kind": "primitive",
                        "props": {
                          "style": {
                            "alignItems": "flex-start",
                            "flexDirection": "row",
                            "marginBottom": 8,
                          },
                        },
                        "tag": "VIEW",
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "When nurses document clinical findings in real time — vital trends, assessment findings, response to treatment — the medical record arrives at CDI review more complete. Specialists may be able to assign a specific, accurate DRG without querying the physician for clarification. Fewer queries means fewer physician interruptions and shorter coding cycles.",
                          },
                        ],
                        "kind": "primitive",
                        "props": {
                          "style": {
                            "color": "#666666",
                            "fontSize": 9,
                            "lineHeight": 1.5,
                            "marginBottom": 10,
                          },
                        },
                        "tag": "TEXT",
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "Signals to track",
                          },
                        ],
                        "kind": "primitive",
                        "props": {
                          "style": {
                            "color": "#1A1A1A",
                            "fontSize": 7.5,
                            "fontWeight": "bold",
                            "letterSpacing": 1.5,
                            "marginBottom": 6,
                            "textTransform": "uppercase",
                          },
                        },
                        "tag": "TEXT",
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "children": [
                                  {
                                    "kind": "text",
                                    "value": "CDI queries per 100 admissions",
